# Terminal Anki — README recording.
#
#   npm run demo        # build, seed a demo collection, record docs/demo.gif
#
# Requires VHS (https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs) and its ttyd/ffmpeg deps.
# The collection it records lives in .demo/ and is generated by
# scripts/seed-demo.mjs, so the whole thing is reproducible: same cards, same
# grid, four cards due.

Output docs/demo.gif

Set Shell bash
Set FontFamily "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font"
Set FontSize 18
Set LineHeight 1.0
Set Width 1000
Set Height 620
Set Padding 20
Set Theme "Dracula"
Set Framerate 25
Set TypingSpeed 15ms

Hide
Type "clear; node scripts/seed-demo.mjs > /dev/null; TERMINAL_ANKI_DATA_DIR=.demo node dist/cli/main.js"
Enter
Sleep 2s
Show

# The menu, with a collection already in use.
Sleep 2000ms

# Study everything due: four cards, two keystrokes each.
Enter
Sleep 1200ms
Enter
Sleep 1200ms

Space
Sleep 1500ms
Type "3"
Sleep 500ms

Sleep 900ms
Space
Sleep 1600ms
Type "4"
Sleep 500ms

Sleep 900ms
Space
Sleep 1500ms
Type "5"
Sleep 500ms

Sleep 900ms
Space
Sleep 1800ms
Type "4"
Sleep 2800ms

# Session summary, then back to the menu.
Enter
Sleep 1000ms

# Analytics: the activity grid, then the session log.
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 400ms
Enter
Sleep 1800ms
Right
Sleep 1300ms
Escape
Sleep 700ms

# Settings, with the theme previewed live on the real frame.
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 90ms
Down
Sleep 500ms
Enter
Sleep 1400ms
Right
Sleep 1400ms
Right
Sleep 1600ms
Enter
Sleep 900ms

# What every key does. Ends on the overlay, which is the last thing to see.
Type "?"
Sleep 2500ms
